    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n101610" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σφαλλός</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σφᾰλός</span></b> , ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>a round leaden plate</i>, which was thrown by a
			strap attached to a ring, a variety of the <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δίσκος</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				8.72
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>a round block of wood</i> with two holes for the feet, <i>pair
				of stocks</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Epich.
				148
			</span></i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σφάκελλος</span> codd. <i><span class="en">
				Ath.
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
			</span></i> l.c., <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σφέλας</span>.</div>
